    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nbasics\n\n### Description\n\nIn vim-unimpaired, you can insert blank lines above and below with `[<space>` and `]<space` similar to `gO` and `go` from mini.basics. However, in vim-unimpaired you can press dot to insert more and more lines after the first `[/]<space>`.\r\n\r\nI would like to have the same behaviour in mini.nvim. In particular for `gO`, where you have to reach for the shift key, dot-repeat is much more ergonomic.",
